problem:
Determine the values of \( z \in \mathbb{C} \) for which \( A_2(z) = 0 \), where \( e^{jz} = A_0(z) + j A_1(z) + j^2 A_2(z) \) and:
\[
\begin{cases}
A_0(z) = \displaystyle \sum_{n \geq 0} \frac{x^{3n}}{(3n)!} \\
A_1(z) = \displaystyle \sum_{n \geq 0} \frac{x^{3n+1}}{(3n+1)!} \\
A_2(z) = \displaystyle \sum_{n \geq 0} \frac{x^{3n+2}}{(3n+2)!}
\end{cases}
\]
with \( j = e^{i \frac{2\pi}{3}} \).
